WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:04.400
<i>MOUNT MIYAMA SHOPPING TOWN</i>

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.900
Pork cutlets, croquettes,

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.530
ginger-fried pork...

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.700
Meat and potatoes, sukiyaki...

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.660
Roasted tofu...

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.240
Mackerel... saury...

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.450
Red snapper!

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.040
And it's over my budget!

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.260
Pork cutlets, croquettes...

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.970
Red snapper and flounder!

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.640
Natural red sea bream!

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.140
<i>BIG FISH FESTIVAL</i>

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.480
And they're all killer deals!

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.670
Well, hey, it's you, kid!

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.260
You, uh, working part-time here?

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:57.340
Yeah, isn't it obvious?

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.180
So you do all the cooking, kid?

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:01.890
Well, yeah. Something wrong with that?

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.850
There's nothing wrong with it, but...

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.520
Excuse me, young man.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.980
What would you recommend today?

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.480
I've got some great red snapper today!

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.150
Young lady!

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.990
Young lady? Go on with you!

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.240
Fine, I'll take some red snapper.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.120
At your service!

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.200
The great Celtic hero, peddling fish...

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:29.170
I think I'd rather have fish for dinner after all.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:32.670
Lancer!

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.300
Huh?

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.510
Which of these is affordable?

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.930
Let's see...

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.140
How about salmon?

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.560
It's cheap! Plus it's good!

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.310
Salmon, huh? Sounds good.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.770
That would taste great steamed, huh?

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.440
All right! Tonight's dinner will be salmon baked in foil!

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.900
What's that? Does that taste good?

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.950
I'd say it's pretty good for such an easy meal.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.410
Give me three, will you?

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.590
Hey, you gave me one extra.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.130
Hey, kid, let me try some of that, too!

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.300
Don't worry!

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.510
I'm paying for my own share!

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.640
Um, that's not what I mean...

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.230
So long! I'll be heading over later, so go get dinner ready!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:45.780
What's this?

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:55.630
It's coming from here.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:02.840
Oh?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.350
Who knew you'd be greeting me, Saber?

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:09.140
I came this way because I sensed magical powers.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.020
What are you doing here?

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.230
Oh, the kid hasn't told you?

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.980
I came here for dinner.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.730
D-Dinner?

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.400
Pardon me!

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:24.820
Here you go!

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.120
Whoa!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.040
Thanks for going to the trouble.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.540
Hey, this is sake!

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:35.170
What? You mean you can't drink?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.540
I'm a minor, remember?

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.920
Ah, don't sweat the little things, okay?

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.550
Or you'll never get bigger!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.260
Okay, then, I'm gonna
make myself at home until dinner.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.600
I guess we'll have to give this to Fuji-nee.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.700
Come to think of it,

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.830
Ireland's famous for salmon, right?

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.580
Wasn't there some kind of Celtic myth...

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.590
...called "Fionn mac Cumhaill and
the Salmon of Knowledge" or something?

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:23.590
All right, then!

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:35.480
First,

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.360
before seasoning, sprinkle the fillets with a little sake,

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.440
and salt them lightly on both sides.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.320
Then let them marinate for five to ten minutes.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.280
Once the moisture is drawn out,

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.660
wipe them down with paper towels.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.040
Next up, the onions.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.540
Cut them into thin slices.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.630
Do the same for the carrots.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.670
Separate the shimeji mushrooms.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.550
Then season the salmon with salt and pepper.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:09.890
<i>ALUMINUM FOIL</i>

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.850
Spread the onions and carrots,

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.560
sprinkle them with finely ground consommé,

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.480
then after you've placed the
salmon and mushrooms on top,

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.900
top it all off with a chunk of butter.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.030
Seal both ends of the foil,

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.240
and close the lid.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.200
Then steam on low heat for 15 to 20 minutes.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:35.200
And now, two side dishes and soup...

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.000
Lancer?

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.170
Huh?

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:45.170
I have to ask you again.
What brought you here out of the blue?

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:48.720
Like I said before... dinner. Dinner!

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:52.180
Don't make such a scary face!

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:58.100
See, I remember how the Matou girl
and Rider raved about the kid's cooking

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:02.610
when they dropped by the other day.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.610
That's a fact. Shirou's cooking is delicious after all.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.160
In that case, it can't be helped.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.780
Let us have dinner together tonight.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.620
What's this?

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.460
Are you saying I need the King of
Knights' permission to have your cooking?

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:21.670
Oh, no.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.720
I'm home!

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:32.720
Hey!

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.220
It's Big Sis Taiga!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:36.810
Hey!

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:39.890
Is that you, Lancer? Why are you here?

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:42.350
Yay!

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:42.350
I'm here as a guest for dinner.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.980
Dinner will be ready soon, so sit down!

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:00.750
For the finishing touch,

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.580
garnish with parsley.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.220
Um...

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.800
I'll be serving salmon baked in foil tonight.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:19.430
Here you go!

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.520
So that's what it looks like.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.020
Okay, then, I'm digging in!

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.210
This is good! I like how you seasoned it!

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:45.830
Huh? What's this?

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.880
This is wasabi mayonnaise.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:51.760
I made a batch for tonight.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:54.590
I think it'll enhance the flavor in a different way.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.140
Yeah?

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.520
Hey! This is pretty damn good!

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.230
Shirou, let me have some, too!

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.480
Okay, okay.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:25.580
And you were acting all stuck-up not five minutes ago!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.430
What can I say?

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:46.690
Thanks for the meal!

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:52.690
Oh, man!

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.280
That was amazing!

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:55.820
Good for you, kid!

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:02.120
Since I'm a Servant,
normally, I don't need to eat at all, but...

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.750
I like a good meal!

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.290
Let's do this again!

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:09.290
Yeah.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:20.760
Here you go.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.020
Okay.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:31.360
Come on, haven't you heard of
"appreciation for meal and lodging"?

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:36.400
Well, but, "lodging" means you're gonna spend the night!

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:38.860
Man, you get so uptight over every little thing!

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:40.660
Who are you calling uptight?

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:42.660
There!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.790
Now that we're done cleaning up...

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.290
What do you say we get hammered?

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.630
Hey, you've got a lot!

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.340
No, no, no!

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.300
Wanna keep going until morning?

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:56.170
Bring it!

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:57.510
T-Taiga!

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.680
What, you're not going home?
